Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:42:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/34] upstream: Flash Next at --tp 2, PR #1784 (laudney) as
 this series carries it

Upstream TensorFold PR #1784 by laudney: --tp 2 for the CUDA families with ranks, the ranks' checkpoint digest,
BF16 dense and shared layers and FP8 n-gram rows and MTP experts in ModelOpt checkpoints, one GPU's expert sums at
--tp 2, and exact output-column splits. This is the PR's head of 2026-11-02 merged onto upstream main 089a18dff;
upstream later merged a revised version of the same PR into main. Every later patch in this series is built on it.
Not written by us: the authorship stays laudney's.

Its commits (subject, then the matching upstream main commit where its subject is on main):
- fix(flashnext): keep the ranked vtable static [95453c567ea5]
- feat(cuda): serve --tp to the CUDA families with ranks [1e7f5dbacdba]
- feat(flashnext): ranks agree on a computed checkpoint digest [d6b3e6ee5b92]
- feat(flashnext): accept BF16 dense and shared layers in ModelOpt [bfc2cc4ea6d2]
- feat(flashnext): FP8 rows in the n-gram table [89a6600fff6c]
- feat(flashnext): FP8 block experts in the MTP head [9b6d86569592]
- docs(flashnext): serve NVIDIA's NVFP4 checkpoint at TP=2 [7e4c02d53e4c]
- refactor(cuda): keep --tp's refusals and test out of cuda.zig [a1f124b5a183]
- test(contract): gate Flash Next NVFP4's BF16 and FP8 expert kernels [e516442dfeb0]
- fix(flashnext): keep one GPU's expert sums at --tp 2 [2676a568c2cb]
- docs(changelog): note --tp 2 replies equal one GPU's for Flash Next [afb82937e7bd]
- style(contract): shorten comments for the lean rule [6afbcdc99900]
- fix(flashnext): word the --tp load refusals and credit the PR [00db33f55749]
- feat(flashnext): split dense output columns with exact gathers [cf63ff641bf3]
- test(cuda): compare GDN heads against a frozen baseline [537d77606983]

Flags this patch adds (a flag's default is its unset value; unset leaves the engine as it was
before the flag, and a knob named under another flag only matters when that flag is on):
- TF_FLASHNEXT_SPLIT_DENSE: unset or 1 splits, 0 keeps every dense projection whole.
